menu "BundleFS"

    config BUNDLEFS_BLOCK_MAP_BUDGET_KIB
        int "BundleFS Catalog block-map RAM budget per store (KiB)"
        range 16 16384
        default 1024
        help
            When a store is formatted, the data block defaults to the medium's own
            unit (erase sector or MMU page) and is doubled only while the Catalog
            block map (4 bytes per data block, kept in RAM while mounted) would
            exceed this budget. Mounting adopts whatever block size the committed
            Catalog records; this value only affects fresh formats.
endmenu
